; a Byte AND, OR or EOR of operands of different sign (#1218, #1217): the
; port's byte operation is a Word operation, so no stale upper byte
; (-2 AND 0 is $FF00, 3 OR -2 is $00FF in the original's and.b, or.b) is
; widened as part of the value; every line prints 1 (true).  AmiBlitz3
; v3.14.0 keeps the stale byte of the variable forms (the outputs 1, 3, 5 and 6
; print 0 there, tests/ab3/cli/byte_bitop_stale.ref.expect)
mb.b=-2 : zb.b=0 : tb.b=3 : ob.b=1
zw.w=0 : mw.w=-1 : z.l=0 : r.l=0
If (mb AND zb)=zw Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
If (-2 AND 0)=zw Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
If (mb AND zb)+zw=0 Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
If ((-2 AND 0) LSL 1)=0 Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
If (tb OR mb)=mw Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
If (ob EOR mb)=mw Then NPrint 1 Else NPrint 0
r=(0=(-2 AND 0)) : NPrint r+2
r=(z=(mb AND zb)) : NPrint r+2
r=(3<(3 OR -2)) : NPrint r+1
End
